w.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Netherlands and France have moved their gold out of US vaults. Part of the reason is fears about the reliability of the US, but equally important is the need to keep gold closer to home in the event of a crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Several killed in series of Russian strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27edd122fe23e9ca6273f659311c165236e6e42341bc2e6bbc96546f63d21fba</id><updated>2026-09-14T05:08:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-several-killed-in-series-of-russian-strikes/a-79245980--1c9c8b0bb81c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-several-killed-in-series-of-russian-strikes/a-79245980?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Local authorities said several civilians were killed and dozens more wounded across Ukraine by Russian strikes. Meanwhile, the Kremlin has rejected Volodymyr Zelenskyy's proposal to meet with the Russian leader in Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria: Fire at factory making munitions for Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cea039377707fb4e530c70d01ccb86f9fb06f7b2913616a7b0c0be08b1b1578f</id><updated>2026-09-14T05:08:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T12:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-fire-at-factory-making-munitions-for-ukraine/a-79245062--ffd8d661930f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-fire-at-factory-making-munitions-for-ukraine/a-79245062?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgarian authorities are investigating a fire at a munitions factory for links to an explosion at a similar facility in August. Arms maker EMCO says no human error was involved, as investigators look at sabotage.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump visits Ireland, says unification would be 'fantastic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:026a8add63a6605b2b27ee73176d6551fb61a1447cedd29ea187603bdcc430c0</id><updated>2026-09-14T05:08:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685--23dd10281a51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's trip to Ireland to watch a golf tournament has also included meetings with leaders there.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda lays 'boy king' Oyo to rest amid succession row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a33af0135fc0218754ee43ecf908c5fc5443f823a8a6aea67709467ec52d0a75</id><updated>2026-09-14T05:08:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-lays-boy-king-oyo-to-rest-amid-succession-row/a-79243428--755cb45ab2c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-lays-boy-king-oyo-to-rest-amid-succession-row/a-79243428?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uganda has buried King Oyo Nyimba, who was crowned in the Tooro Kingdom in 1995 aged just 3. His death at 34 has triggered a dispute over a successor, as rumors abound of possible heirs born out of wedlock.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS summit leaders urge 'maximum restraint' in Middle East</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63fbdd7e4840778d6a66b01901c07ae2db0fa41232469b61cca654063387dd91</id><updated>2026-09-14T05:08:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-leaders-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east/live-79224239--4541a165cd4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-leaders-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east/live-79224239?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The joint declaration at the BRICS 2026 summit expressed 'deep concern' over hostilities in the Middle East. China's President Xi Jinping said the Iran war was not in the bloc's interest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian GRU spies behind failed Leipzig attack: reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e35bfec078c46ec24669e15247c5853e77fbe4e5bf0e50a4461ef9c6eca18b5d</id><updated>2026-09-14T05:08:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858--97143d694fa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A German newspaper has cited reports tying a failed attack at Leipzig Airport to Moscow's GRU military intelligence agency. One suspect's ties to GRU were known when he entered the country, yet he was not surveilled.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
